<BaseLayout title="Privacy — NMA Ogun" description="How the NMA Ogun public website handles browsing and links to separate member services.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Your information matters." description="Information about browsing the Nigerian Medical Association, Ogun State Branch website." />
  <section class="container page-section prose"><h2>Browsing this website</h2><p>This website is provided by the Nigerian Medical Association, Ogun State Branch. It does not include analytics, advertising trackers, a membership database connection or an enquiry submission form. Website code does not set cookies or store information in your browser.</p><h2>Hosting and security</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts and delivers this website. Delivering and protecting a website involves processing connection information, which can include IP addresses, requested addresses and request times. No website-specific enquiry records or visitor profiles are created by this application. Worker request logging is disabled in this website’s deployment configuration. Cloudflare may process operational and security data under its own service arrangements.</p><h2>Images and fonts</h2><p>Photographs and fonts are served with the website. No embedded map, social media widget or third-party font request is used.</p><h2>Member services</h2><p>Sign-in, registration and account recovery links take you to the separate NMA Ogun member portal. Information entered there is handled by that service. Review the portal’s guidance before submitting personal information. Do not submit patient information through membership or general website channels.</p><h2>Privacy questions</h2><p>Raise privacy questions with the NMA Ogun secretariat through your established association contact channel. This public website currently has no enquiry form or published email address. Any future enquiry service will need its own clear information about collection, use and retention.</p><p>Last updated: 16 October 2026.</p><a class="text-link" href="/membership">Member service guidance <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
